  "label": "User projected onto the textual material describing the financial consequence of theft",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'your purchase of $19.99 comes to $21.36 after theft' because the phrase 'your purchase' directly addresses the viewer, making the user the subject of the transaction and the implied victim or observer of the absurd situation. The user is positioned as the one who would experience or be affected by this cost increase, thereby projecting them onto the textual material.",
